<<<
&la. The sex of the person whose name is introduced by this does not affect the form, la agreeing not with it but with an omitted modes: a la reine; a la (not. au) mattre-@hotel;
===
**à la.** The sex of the person whose name is introduced by this does not affect the form, *la* agreeing not with it but with an omitted *mode*: *à la reine*; *à la* (not. *au*) *maître-d'hôtel*;
>>>

<<<
a@ Home-rule Bill a la (not au) Gladstone.
===
*a Home-rule Bill à la* (not *au*) *Gladstone.*
>>>

